{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/797102-how-about-giving-permanent-anathemas-at-lair-6","id":797102,"title":"How About Giving Permanent Anathemas At Lair 6+?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-30T17:59:17-08:00","id":797102,"title":"How About Giving Permanent Anathemas At Lair 6+?","content":"I'm just worried that maybe this is going against the spirit of the game. It possibly gives too much validity to the Heroes' belief that Beasts are no different from the monsters of the typical monomyth, instead of making Anathemas a plain dirty trick.<br /> <br /> If that's not a problem, how does one determine the intensity of these Anathemas at a given time? The temporary ones become less intense in proportion to how low the Beast's Satiety is at the moment they are placed. If that were true for the permanent ones, players would probably not consider a play style focused on keeping Satiety high to have stronger Nightmares, which would be a pity. And if I remember correctly, Incarnate Beasts are immune to Anathemas, and that Inheritance has a prerequisite of Lair 8+. How can I get around these issues?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-31T04:02:36-08:00","id":797269,"title":"","content":"I don't think it is too much against the spirit of the game, really. Anathema are basically just specialized Banes and Bans. Everything non-mortal in the CoD tends to have them, and I'd argue that &quot;lack of air, nurishment or blood&quot; could count as a bane for humans too. Hells, Horrors are basically goetic entites, and they have Banes and Bans too.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't think its too much against the spirit of the game to give the Begotten Anathema from Character Creation. Its a bit of an issue at high Satiety, when the characters are closer to acting like mortals with some psychic abilities, but completely in theme at low Satiety. I had a PC that I had start with an Atavism - they were too scared to drop to Starving to get rid of it. You're literally <i>dying</i> at that point, so the character bore the Atavism as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Incarnate Beasts are like vampire Methusalah, ascending to become a spirit totem, or Archmage. You don't worry about them, because that's an end game scenario.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;wanting High Satiety&quot; issue? I think you're also borrowing trouble here. Low Satiety Beasts tend to feed heavily by relying on their Hungers, while High Satiety Beasts tend to use a lot of Family Dinners - its simply too difficult to feed your Hunger while maintaining a High Satiety. And, frankly, its entirely thematically appropriate for a Beast that maintains High Satiety to be practically immune to Anathema. Low Satiety Beasts have to occasionally rise up to Mid Satiety as a matter of course - its a requirement. And that's when the Heroes strike. High Satiety Beasts never have to dip into Mid Satiety, so they never have to become vulnerable to Anathema. Furthermore, High Satiety Beasts tend to not engage in behavior that attracts Heroes in the first place. There's a reason why I suggest thinking of Satiety as the Integrity equivalent.<br /> <br /> As for your worry that players will favor High Satiety play? I doubt that will be an issue. People play their concepts. If someone wants to play a fearsome dragon archetype, they're not going to want to focus on Nightmares and Family Dinner, acting like Sookie Stackhouse - they're going to want a grandoise Lair, feed their Collection Hunger, and a suite of appropriate Atavisms.<br /> <br /> <br /> I honestly think you're just borrowing trouble here. It should be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-31-2015, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}